{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40661","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65972","text":"Slice B, Commit 3 — the "},{"id":"spn-65973","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-65974","text":" surface: closure memo"}]},{"id":"blk-40662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65975","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-65976","text":" CLOSED. "},{"id":"spn-65977","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run48"},{"id":"spn-65978","text":" PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (6s, 71 rows). "},{"id":"spn-65979","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate48"},{"id":"spn-65980","text":" "},{"id":"spn-65981","marks":["bold"],"text":"19/19 ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"spn-65982","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-65983","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep"},{"id":"spn-65984","text":" "},{"id":"spn-65985","marks":["bold"],"text":"16/16 green"},{"id":"spn-65986","text":" (141s, reference + native), L-0 tier unmoved."}]},{"id":"blk-40663","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65987","text":"Commit 2 gave a route a canonical form and an identity but no spelling. Commit 3 gives it the ruled spelling in both directions:"}]},{"id":"blk-40664","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb] (body=0.0.0.7)"},{"id":"blk-40665","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65988","text":"and closes the two things that spelling makes reachable — the Q4 writer-15 reservation, and a silent world substitution in the authoring draft."}]},{"id":"blk-40666","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65989","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40668","spans":[{"id":"spn-65990","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-40669","spans":[{"id":"spn-65991","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-40667","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40670","spans":[{"id":"spn-65992","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40671","spans":[{"id":"spn-65993","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_RE"},{"id":"spn-65994","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65995","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_KEYS"},{"id":"spn-65996","text":", "},{"id":"spn-65997","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-65998","text":", the route branch in "},{"id":"spn-65999","marks":["code"],"text":"_parse_core_permissive"},{"id":"spn-66000","text":"; bootstrap "},{"id":"spn-66001","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66002","text":" message split off from "},{"id":"spn-66003","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-66004","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-66005","marks":["code"],"text":"=="}]}],[{"id":"blk-40672","spans":[{"id":"spn-66006","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40673","spans":[{"id":"spn-66007","text":"route section emitted after the edges, "},{"id":"spn-66008","marks":["code"],"text":"_emit_body"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40674","spans":[{"id":"spn-66009","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_canonical.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40675","spans":[{"id":"spn-66010","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_ROUTE_WRITER_RESERVED"},{"id":"spn-66011","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66012","marks":["code"],"text":"routes_of_artifact"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40676","spans":[{"id":"spn-66013","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40677","spans":[{"id":"spn-66014","marks":["code"],"text":"check_route_writer_reservation"},{"id":"spn-66015","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66016","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40678","spans":[{"id":"spn-66017","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_draft.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40679","spans":[{"id":"spn-66018","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-66019","text":", the computed "},{"id":"spn-66020","marks":["code"],"text":"_draft_loss"},{"id":"spn-66021","text":" round-trip, both draft doors"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40680","spans":[{"id":"spn-66022","marks":["code"],"text":"spinner_bench.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40681","spans":[{"id":"spn-66023","text":"call site widened to the composed door"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40682","spans":[{"id":"spn-66024","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40683","spans":[{"id":"spn-66025","text":"closing NOTE corrected (it said \"there is no "},{"id":"spn-66026","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66027","text":" surface\")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40684","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66028","text":"The parser's job stops at "},{"id":"spn-66029","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"this line says a route.\""},{"id":"spn-66030","text":" Endpoint roles, the one-shot source law, the body range, duplicates and the budget are all the seal's, and they are the seal's for a route arriving from "},{"id":"spn-66031","marks":["bold"],"text":"any"},{"id":"spn-66032","text":" surface. Every Q7 row proves this twice: the parse "},{"id":"spn-66033","marks":["bold"],"text":"succeeds"},{"id":"spn-66034","text":" and the seal "},{"id":"spn-66035","marks":["bold"],"text":"refuses"},{"id":"spn-66036","text":". A parser that had helpfully re-implemented one of these fails the first half."}]},{"id":"blk-40685","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66037","text":"2. Five autonomous decisions — please confirm or overrule"}]},{"id":"blk-40686","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66038","text":"(a) The draft "},{"id":"spn-66039","marks":["bold"],"text":"REFUSES"},{"id":"spn-66040","text":" route-bearing worlds rather than being widened"}]},{"id":"blk-40687","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66041","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-66042","marks":["code"],"text":"WorldDraft"},{"id":"spn-66043","text":" stores a world as "},{"id":"spn-66044","marks":["code"],"text":"(objects, edges)"},{"id":"spn-66045","text":". A route is neither, so it was invisible. "},{"id":"spn-66046","marks":["bold"],"text":"Measured before the guard was written:"},{"id":"spn-66047","text":" opening the one-route world for editing produced no error and yielded "},{"id":"spn-66048","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-d3e555be…"},{"id":"spn-66049","text":" — the route-free twin, a perfectly good world with a perfectly good id. Legal, which is what makes it dangerous."}]},{"id":"blk-40688","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66050","text":"Widening the draft to carry routes is not a language change: it is a new revision of "},{"id":"spn-66051","marks":["bold"],"text":"every persisted authoring document"},{"id":"spn-66052","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-66053","marks":["code"],"text":"ForgeProjectV2"},{"id":"spn-66054","text":", the v0.6-0 recovery journal, the draft-state ledger, the canvas reconciler. That is a document-format migration and it does not belong inside a language slice, so commit 3 ships a "},{"id":"spn-66055","marks":["bold"],"text":"refusal"},{"id":"spn-66056","text":" and defers the widening."}]},{"id":"blk-40689","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66057","text":"The guard is a "},{"id":"spn-66058","marks":["bold"],"text":"computed round-trip"},{"id":"spn-66059","text":", not a construct blacklist:"}]},{"id":"blk-40690","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"want = W.lower_graph(g).semantic_artifact_id\ngot, err = _seal(objects, edges, profile)\nif err is None and got == want: return None      # nothing was lost"},{"id":"blk-40691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66060","text":"It names no construct, so it will refuse the "},{"id":"spn-66061","marks":["italic"],"text":"next"},{"id":"spn-66062","text":" unrepresentable construct without being edited — the same property that made "},{"id":"spn-66063","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_legacy.export_canvas_graph_v1"},{"id":"spn-66064","text":" learn about routes on its own."}]},{"id":"blk-40692","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66065","text":"(b) The loss refusal reports "},{"id":"spn-66066","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"}]},{"id":"blk-40693","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66067","marks":["code"],"text":"REPLACE_STATUS"},{"id":"spn-66068","text":" has four frozen terminal values. "},{"id":"spn-66069","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"},{"id":"spn-66070","text":" is the only one whose "},{"id":"spn-66071","marks":["bold"],"text":"behaviour"},{"id":"spn-66072","text":" is exactly this case (refused, draft untouched, nothing for the author to repair). It is an imperfect "},{"id":"spn-66073","marks":["italic"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-66074","text":"; the diagnostic carries the honest code "},{"id":"spn-66075","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-66076","text":". Inventing a fifth status is a change to a published contract, not a language decision — hence the deferral."}]},{"id":"blk-40694","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66077","text":"(c) Routes emit "},{"id":"spn-66078","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-66079","text":" the edges, not interleaved"}]},{"id":"blk-40695","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66080","text":"Sorting a route into edge order would need one comparison key spanning two vocabularies, and the two orderings are canonical for different reasons: an edge's order is "},{"id":"spn-66081","marks":["bold"],"text":"presentational"},{"id":"spn-66082","text":", a route's order "},{"id":"spn-66083","marks":["bold"],"text":"IS its minted ADMIT `sequence`"},{"id":"spn-66084","text":" (Q4). Interleaving would make an identity-bearing order look like a formatting choice. A route-free world therefore emits "},{"id":"spn-66085","marks":["italic"],"text":"exactly"},{"id":"spn-66086","text":" the pre-Slice-B text — no separator, no empty section (proved by "},{"id":"spn-66087","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5d"},{"id":"spn-66088","text":", see §3)."}]},{"id":"blk-40696","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66089","text":"(d) "},{"id":"spn-66090","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"},{"id":"spn-66091","text":" composes binding + reservation into one door"}]},{"id":"blk-40697","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66092","text":"Both halves stay callable by name, but production goes through the composed door, because the failure mode of two independent checks is that a call site grows one and not the other — and the forgotten half is whichever was added second. Today that is the reservation. "},{"id":"spn-66093","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8i"},{"id":"spn-66094","text":" and mutation "},{"id":"spn-66095","marks":["bold"],"text":"M16"},{"id":"spn-66096","text":" are the rows that hold this."}]},{"id":"blk-40698","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66097","text":"(e) The bootstrap DSL gets "},{"id":"spn-66098","marks":["bold"],"text":"no"},{"id":"spn-66099","text":" route directive"}]},{"id":"blk-40699","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66100","text":"It is a frozen migration bridge. Its "},{"id":"spn-66101","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66102","text":" rejection was corrected, though: it used to say "},{"id":"spn-66103","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"a transition class, not an IR v1 edge\""},{"id":"spn-66104","text":", which is now false twice over — a route "},{"id":"spn-66105","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-66106","text":" an IR v1.1 construct, and it was never an edge (D8). It now points at the surface that does have one. "},{"id":"spn-66107","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-66108","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66109","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-66110","text":" keep the old message. This is the identical correction commit 1 made for "},{"id":"spn-66111","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-66112","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40700","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66113","text":"3. What the mutation round found"}]},{"id":"blk-40701","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66114","text":"Three survivors on the first pass, all three real. Recorded because they are the useful part."}]},{"id":"blk-40702","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66115","marks":["bold"],"text":"M9 — the route separator emitted unconditionally. SURVIVED with nothing red."},{"id":"spn-66116","text":" The most useful finding. Whitespace is non-semantic, so no identity moved and "},{"id":"spn-66117","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5"},{"id":"spn-66118","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-66119","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5b"},{"id":"spn-66120","text":" stayed green. And the formatter is "},{"id":"spn-66121","marks":["code"],"text":"graph -> text"},{"id":"spn-66122","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-66123","marks":["code"],"text":"text -> text"},{"id":"spn-66124","text":", so the extra blank line is a "},{"id":"spn-66125","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed point"},{"id":"spn-66126","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-66127","marks":["code"],"text":"Q3b"},{"id":"spn-66128","text":" (idempotence) stayed green too; the prediction that it would catch this was simply wrong. Meanwhile the canonical "},{"id":"spn-66129","marks":["bold"],"text":"bytes"},{"id":"spn-66130","text":" of every route-free world in the tree had moved — the exact law "},{"id":"spn-66131","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format"},{"id":"spn-66132","text":"'s own comment claims (\"no blank separator, no empty section\") and which nothing checked. "},{"id":"spn-66133","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q5d` exists because of this line"},{"id":"spn-66134","text":", and states the law structurally (a route-free world's text ends at its last edge) rather than pinning a literal, which would fork the emitter."}]},{"id":"blk-40703","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66135","marks":["bold"],"text":"M11 — `replace_world_source`'s guard removed. `Q9e` stayed green."},{"id":"spn-66136","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66137","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-66138","text":" claims \"the draft is UNTOUCHED\". True, but for the wrong reason: the route-free twin of that source "},{"id":"spn-66139","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-66140","text":" the draft's current world, so a missing guard falls through to the semantic-noop branch and leaves revision 0 with the right candidate. "},{"id":"spn-66141","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-66142","text":" is structurally unable to tell "},{"id":"spn-66143","marks":["italic"],"text":"refused"},{"id":"spn-66144","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-66145","marks":["italic"],"text":"silently accepted as a no-op"},{"id":"spn-66146","text":". "},{"id":"spn-66147","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q9h`/`Q9i`/`Q9j` were added"},{"id":"spn-66148","text":": a paste whose lost world is a "},{"id":"spn-66149","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-66150","text":" world (two mailboxes + a route), plus a vacuity check that the twin really does differ."}]},{"id":"blk-40704","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66151","marks":["bold"],"text":"M14 — the reservation widened to every world. Reported as \"Q8 raised\"."},{"id":"spn-66152","text":" Not a production defect but a reporting one: "},{"id":"spn-66153","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-66154","text":" raised, and "},{"id":"spn-66155","marks":["code"],"text":"section()"},{"id":"spn-66156","text":" renamed the failure after its neighbour — so a reservation made too "},{"id":"spn-66157","marks":["bold"],"text":"strong"},{"id":"spn-66158","text":" read as a reservation that was "},{"id":"spn-66159","marks":["bold"],"text":"broken"},{"id":"spn-66160","text":". "},{"id":"spn-66161","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-66162","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-66163","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8c"},{"id":"spn-66164","text":" are callables now and keep their own names. (This is the same lesson as run47's \"many laws share one error code\": a row must be identifiable as itself when it fails.)"}]},{"id":"blk-40705","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66165","text":"Also worth recording: "},{"id":"spn-66166","marks":["bold"],"text":"M5"},{"id":"spn-66167","text":" (body arity forked onto "},{"id":"spn-66168","marks":["code"],"text":"_rotor_dots"},{"id":"spn-66169","text":") is caught only at section granularity, and "},{"id":"spn-66170","marks":["code"],"text":"Q1d"},{"id":"spn-66171","text":" cannot see it at all — the rotor message happens to contain the same "},{"id":"spn-66172","marks":["code"],"text":"\"must have 4 lanes\""},{"id":"spn-66173","text":" while saying "},{"id":"spn-66174","marks":["italic"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-66175","text":" about a "},{"id":"spn-66176","marks":["italic"],"text":"body"},{"id":"spn-66177","text":". That is exactly the drift "},{"id":"spn-66178","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-66179","text":"'s docstring refuses, and it is why the two 4s are not one constant."}]},{"id":"blk-40706","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66180","text":"4. Not frozen"}]},{"id":"blk-40707","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66181","text":"A route can now be "},{"id":"spn-66182","marks":["bold"],"text":"written, canonicalized, sealed, formatted, and refused for every reason it should be"},{"id":"spn-66183","text":" — and it still does nothing at runtime. Commit 4 folds it. Freeze the Slice B line after Commit 4, then promote "},{"id":"spn-66184","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66185","text":" to Grounded in "},{"id":"spn-66186","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-66187","text":" §14."}]},{"id":"blk-40708","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66188","text":"Carried obligation into Commit 4: unify "},{"id":"spn-66189","marks":["code"],"text":"route_body_in_range"},{"id":"spn-66190","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-66191","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-66192","text":" to remove the fork (the obligation is written into the function's docstring)."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierap732uqz3yfagjy7dxtr625cgoafwq5x45oxqu4dyzcrfeg3rbhsa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}